00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:29.740
Now here is something most retail investors get wrong and it cost me money before I figured it out.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:36.800
Imagine you bought a TSX listed industrial name last week after it bounced from the 200-day

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:43.260
moving average on heavy volume. Your order filled at the ask yet the next candle closed below

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:49.420
that average because the 50-day line was already sloping downward. The mechanism here is simple.

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:56.860
Support levels only hold when volume exceeds the 20-day average and RSI-14 stays above 40.

00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:03.380
Otherwise the bounce is a liquidity grab. Professionals always check the slope of the 50-day versus

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:09.660
the 200-day before treating any test as valid. The biggest mistake retail traders make is

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:15.920
treating every support touch as an automatic buy. Instead always require both a volume spike

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:22.600
and RSI confirmation before entering. Before we wrap, open your brokerage platform tomorrow

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:27.700
and check the 14-day RSI on Bitcoin to decide where to set your price alert.

